<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Felsenweg 6 – Teufelsschlucht — Complete Felsenweiher–Teufelsschlucht–Schweineställe circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>This roughly 18.2 km sandstone loop near Ernzen and Irrel starts at the Felsenweiher parking-road approach. Visit Felsenweiher, walk through Stubenlay to Kuckuckslay’s small bastion on exterior ground, then continue via Liborius chapel through the full northern Teufelsschlucht and quarry paths. Cross fields and orchards, pass the southwestern Schweineställe formations and return to Felsenweiher. Crawling through Lochstein is optional and excluded. Steep uneven stairs, damp rock, mud and roots require sure footing and grippy footwear. Avoid ice, heavy rain and storms, allow daylight and obey restrictions. If any required passage is closed, forbidden or unsafe, this complete itinerary is unavailable. Approximate 440 m ascent/descent and 285 minutes are unmeasured planning estimates. Follow signs and current conditions; the map is for planning.

